      "title": "Cuts force World Food Programme to end support for half a million Palestinians in Gaza",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/cuts-world-food-programme-end-support-palestinians-gaza",
      "description": "<p>Two-thirds of population face crisis levels of food insecurity and 200,000 people are in danger of famine</p><p>This winter is likely to deepen hunger for Palestinians in Gaza, after sweeping aid cuts forced the UN’s World Food Programme (WFP) to end support for more than half a million people each month, the agency’s director for Palestine said.</p><p>More than a year after a Trump-brokered ceasefire came into force, promised reconstruction has not begun, there are few jobs and the vast majority in Gaza still rely on aid to eat.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/19/cuts-world-food-programme-end-support-palestinians-gaza\">Continue reading...</a>",
